## flow/common/flow_utils.tcl :: ::part_alias is not validated against the schema
# The alias table is the only place in the engine where a pack's spelling
# appears, and nothing checks that the names on either side of it are real. A
# dead alias is invisible: `device -> part_name` sat here reading as a promise
# that `part device` returns the full part string, when the schema declares
# `device` as the die and the alias therefore never fired. Removed 2026-09-08,
# found by reading, not by a test.
# part/pack_api.tcl validates its OWN alias table at source time. This second
# table does not, so the next dead alias will be just as invisible.
# FIX: either validate this table against the pack schema at source time, or
# delete it and move its three entries into pack_api.tcl's table - there should
# not be two. Recorded in CONTRACT.md section 8.

## FLOW_MODE=project is the default, and no stage implements it
# CONTRACT.md section 3 declares `project | direct | dfx | protocompiler`, and
# mk/flow.mk:350 defaults to `project`. scripts/fpga-flow-check:1201 DOES
# enum-validate the value, so a typo is refused - that part is right, and `dfx`
# does reach something real (flow/steps/synth_setup.tcl:391 switches synthesis
# to out_of_context for it).
# What is wrong is that `project` NAMES A PATH NOTHING RUNS. flow/vivado/
# 4_synth.tcl:64 says so in its own header: it does not implement `launch_runs
# synth_1`, it runs the in-memory `direct` path whatever the mode says.
# 4_synth.tcl:1056 and 5_impl.tcl:871 record the difference honestly, as a
# NOTCOV line in the stage manifest - which is the right instinct at the wrong
# severity. Every run this toolkit has ever produced declared one flow and
# executed another, and the only place that is visible is a not-covered note.
# `protocompiler` is worse: accepted by the checker, consumed by nothing at all.
# FIX: default to `direct`, since that is what runs, and refuse `project` and
# `protocompiler` in mk/flow.mk until a stage implements them. A declared mode
# that silently maps onto a different one is the class of silent substitution
# this toolkit was built to stop.

